      "rule": "House and garden are designed as one composition: terraces, walls, steps and planting continue the plan outdoors, rather than a garden of a separate, ornamental architectural character. (Contrast the Mediterranean family's working-agricultural-ground idiom, which does not apply here.)",
      "note": "OVERRIDES a cascade fill from mediterranean-vernacular ('the house is inseparable from its working agricultural ground... terraced retaining walls and an axial approach... the aia'), a Tuscan/Italian farm-economy fact with no basis in this style's own text. This node's own defining_characteristics states the actual, well-documented fact directly: 'House and garden designed as one composition, with terraces, walls, steps and planting continuing the plan outdoors' -- the Lutyens/Jekyll partnership is the type case. Fixed here per WP-4.2 instructions rather than on any ancestor kit."
